1655     {\cf20 // Keyboard Modifiers (explicitly submitted by backend via AddKeyEvent() calls)}\par
1656     {\cf20 // - Any functions taking a ImGuiKeyChord parameter can binary-or those with regular keys, e.g. Shortcut(ImGuiMod_Ctrl | ImGuiKey_S).}\par
1657     {\cf20 // - Those are written back into io.KeyCtrl, io.KeyShift, io.KeyAlt, io.KeySuper for convenience,}\par
1658     {\cf20 //   but may be accessed via standard key API such as IsKeyPressed(), IsKeyReleased(), querying duration etc.}\par
1659     {\cf20 // - Code polling every key (e.g. an interface to detect a key press for input mapping) might want to ignore those}\par
1660     {\cf20 //   and prefer using the real keys (e.g. ImGuiKey_LeftCtrl, ImGuiKey_RightCtrl instead of ImGuiMod_Ctrl).}\par
1661     {\cf20 // - In theory the value of keyboard modifiers should be roughly equivalent to a logical or of the equivalent left/right keys.}\par
1662     {\cf20 //   In practice: it's complicated; mods are often provided from different sources. Keyboard layout, IME, sticky keys and}\par
1663     {\cf20 //   backends tend to interfere and break that equivalence. The safer decision is to relay that ambiguity down to the end-user...}\par
