38 {\cf20 // DPI-related helpers (optional)}\par
39 {\cf20 // - Use to enable DPI awareness without having to create an application manifest.}\par
40 {\cf20 // - Your own app may already do this via a manifest or explicit calls. This is mostly useful for our examples/ apps.}\par
41 {\cf20 // - In theory we could call simple functions from Windows SDK such as SetProcessDPIAware(), SetProcessDpiAwareness(), etc.}\par
42 {\cf20 //   but most of the functions provided by Microsoft require Windows 8.1/10+ SDK at compile time and Windows 8/10+ at runtime,}\par
43 {\cf20 //   neither of which we want to require the user to have. So we dynamically select and load those functions to avoid dependencies.}\par
